1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:05,513
Your app is deployed. Then, one morning, it is not answering. Customers get nothing.

2
00:00:06,063 --> 00:00:08,459
Today you work like an engineer on call.

3
00:00:08,459 --> 00:00:09,477
You do not guess.

4
00:00:09,477 --> 00:00:10,794
You read the evidence,

5
00:00:10,794 --> 00:00:11,692
find the cause,

6
00:00:11,692 --> 00:00:12,112
fix it,

7
00:00:12,112 --> 00:00:12,890
and prove it.

8
00:00:13,440 --> 00:00:15,572
Tomcat is broken in three ways.

9
00:00:15,572 --> 00:00:16,809
A wrong Java path.

10
00:00:16,809 --> 00:00:18,941
A port that someone else holds.

11
00:00:18,941 --> 00:00:20,523
And a damaged war file.

12
00:00:21,073 --> 00:00:25,574
You will find each one in the output and the logs, and you will fix them one at a time.

13
00:00:27,124 --> 00:00:30,196
Here is what to expect, from the first minute to the last.

14
00:00:30,746 --> 00:00:33,647
One: Tomcat will not start. You read what it says.

15
00:00:34,197 --> 00:00:38,720
Two: Tomcat starts, but a stranger answers. You find who holds the port.

16
00:00:39,270 --> 00:00:44,518
Three: Tomcat answers, but the app is missing. You read the log, and compare two files.

17
00:00:45,068 --> 00:00:46,902
Four: you act like a customer,

18
00:00:46,902 --> 00:00:48,736
and check that the shop works.

19
00:00:48,736 --> 00:00:50,082
Then your turn: a lab,

20
00:00:50,082 --> 00:00:50,999
with one check.

21
00:00:51,549 --> 00:00:54,855
And one lesson ahead: prove all of it, from a clean copy.

22
00:00:55,405 --> 00:00:57,432
Read it, find it, fix it, prove it.

23
00:00:59,482 --> 00:01:03,663
Before the live part, one method. Every incident, the same five steps.

24
00:01:04,213 --> 00:01:08,715
One: the symptom. What does the customer see? Nothing, an error, the wrong page.

25
00:01:09,265 --> 00:01:14,214
Two: the evidence. The screen output, the log, the port list. Read before you touch.

26
00:01:14,764 --> 00:01:17,580
Three: the cause. One sentence. Write it down.

27
00:01:18,130 --> 00:01:21,629
Four: the fix. The smallest change that removes that cause.

28
00:01:22,179 --> 00:01:27,469
Five: the proof. Ask again, as a customer. Symptom, evidence, cause, fix, proof.

29
00:01:29,019 --> 00:01:34,032
Go to the lab folder.

30
00:01:35,582 --> 00:01:37,481
Look around. Type: L S.

31
00:01:38,031 --> 00:01:40,025
Tomcat is in the tomcat folder.

32
00:01:40,025 --> 00:01:42,920
A good copy of the app is in the good folder.

33
00:01:42,920 --> 00:01:44,657
Something is wrong in here.

34
00:01:44,657 --> 00:01:45,943
We do not know what.

35
00:01:45,943 --> 00:01:46,458
We read.

36
00:01:47,008 --> 00:01:52,320
Start Tomcat, and keep the first two lines.

37
00:01:53,870 --> 00:01:54,722
Symptom one.

38
00:01:54,722 --> 00:01:56,285
Tomcat does not start.

39
00:01:56,285 --> 00:02:00,334
It says: the JAVA_HOME variable is not defined correctly.

40
00:02:00,334 --> 00:02:03,388
And it prints the path it tried: /opt

41
00:02:03,388 --> 00:02:04,880
/java-gone.

42
00:02:04,880 --> 00:02:06,798
That folder does not exist.

43
00:02:07,848 --> 00:02:13,650
Where does that path come from?

44
00:02:14,200 --> 00:02:17,068
Tomcat reads this file before it starts.

45
00:02:17,068 --> 00:02:20,940
Line one sets JAVA_HOME to a folder that is not there.

46
00:02:20,940 --> 00:02:22,732
Write it down: /opt

47
00:02:22,732 --> 00:02:24,238
/java-gone.

48
00:02:24,238 --> 00:02:25,528
That is cause one.

49
00:02:26,078 --> 00:02:31,412
Fix it, with vim.

50
00:02:31,962 --> 00:02:33,951
The wrong line is line one.

51
00:02:33,951 --> 00:02:34,614
Type dd,

52
00:02:34,614 --> 00:02:36,014
to delete the line.

53
00:02:36,014 --> 00:02:36,824
Then colon,

54
00:02:36,824 --> 00:02:37,119
W Q,

55
00:02:37,119 --> 00:02:37,856
and enter,

56
00:02:37,856 --> 00:02:39,108
to save and quit.

57
00:02:39,658 --> 00:02:45,013
Start Tomcat again, and keep the last line.

58
00:02:45,563 --> 00:02:51,558
Tomcat started. Without that line, it finds Java by itself. Fixed? Ask as a customer.

59
00:02:52,108 --> 00:03:02,369
Ask for the health page, and keep two lines.

60
00:03:05,919 --> 00:03:06,763
Symptom two.

61
00:03:06,763 --> 00:03:07,677
Four oh four.

62
00:03:07,677 --> 00:03:11,545
But read the second line: the server is SimpleHTTP,

63
00:03:11,545 --> 00:03:12,037
Python.

64
00:03:12,037 --> 00:03:14,077
This is not Tomcat answering.

65
00:03:14,077 --> 00:03:16,116
Something else owns the port.

66
00:03:16,666 --> 00:03:21,509
Who owns port 8089?

67
00:03:22,059 --> 00:03:25,574
The listener on the port is a program called python3,

68
00:03:25,574 --> 00:03:27,028
with its process number.

69
00:03:27,028 --> 00:03:27,695
A stranger,

70
00:03:27,695 --> 00:03:28,907
sitting on our port.

71
00:03:29,457 --> 00:03:37,436
What does Tomcat say?

72
00:03:37,986 --> 00:03:40,572
Bind exception: address already in use.

73
00:03:40,572 --> 00:03:42,827
Tomcat lost the race for the port.

74
00:03:42,827 --> 00:03:44,949
The log and the port list agree.

75
00:03:44,949 --> 00:03:47,138
Cause two: a python3 server.

76
00:03:47,688 --> 00:03:53,746
Stop the stranger, by its command line.

77
00:03:54,296 --> 00:03:54,617
Quiet.

78
00:03:54,617 --> 00:03:56,649
Dash F matches the whole command line,

79
00:03:56,649 --> 00:03:58,894
and -u keeps it to your own processes.

80
00:03:58,894 --> 00:04:00,177
Tomcat is still running,

81
00:04:00,177 --> 00:04:01,567
but it never got the port.

82
00:04:01,567 --> 00:04:02,316
So restart it.

83
00:04:02,316 --> 00:04:02,583
Stop,

84
00:04:02,583 --> 00:04:03,171
then start.

85
00:04:03,721 --> 00:04:09,076
Stop Tomcat.

86
00:04:09,626 --> 00:04:14,980
Start Tomcat.

87
00:04:15,530 --> 00:04:25,792
Ask again, and keep two lines.

88
00:04:29,342 --> 00:04:29,818
Better.

89
00:04:29,818 --> 00:04:32,741
This four oh four comes from Tomcat itself.

90
00:04:32,741 --> 00:04:33,897
The port is ours.

91
00:04:33,897 --> 00:04:35,665
Now the app: Tomcat is up,

92
00:04:35,665 --> 00:04:37,704
but CloudCart is not running.

93
00:04:38,254 --> 00:04:43,886
Search the log for the cause.

94
00:04:44,436 --> 00:04:47,266
Zip exception: zip end header not found.

95
00:04:47,266 --> 00:04:49,034
A war file is a zip file.

96
00:04:49,034 --> 00:04:50,449
This one has no end.

97
00:04:50,449 --> 00:04:51,651
It was cut short.

98
00:04:51,651 --> 00:04:52,500
Cause three.

99
00:04:53,050 --> 00:05:04,080
Compare the two war files by size.

100
00:05:04,630 --> 00:05:07,628
One hundred thousand bytes in the deployed file.

101
00:05:07,628 --> 00:05:10,564
Almost three hundred thousand in the good copy.

102
00:05:10,564 --> 00:05:13,312
The deployed war is a third of the real one.

103
00:05:13,862 --> 00:05:22,374
Put the good file in place.

104
00:05:22,924 --> 00:05:31,180
Wait, then ask for the health page.

105
00:05:36,730 --> 00:05:37,444
Status up,

106
00:05:37,444 --> 00:05:39,727
version zero point two point oh.

107
00:05:39,727 --> 00:05:41,724
Tomcat noticed the new file,

108
00:05:41,724 --> 00:05:43,722
and redeployed it by itself.

109
00:05:43,722 --> 00:05:44,436
Now check,

110
00:05:44,436 --> 00:05:45,434
as a customer.

111
00:05:45,984 --> 00:05:58,592
Count the products a customer can see.

112
00:05:59,142 --> 00:06:00,134
Twelve products.

113
00:06:00,134 --> 00:06:01,187
The shop is open,

114
00:06:01,187 --> 00:06:02,922
and the catalog is complete.

115
00:06:02,922 --> 00:06:04,966
That is the proof for a customer.

116
00:06:05,516 --> 00:06:09,250
Write the answers, with vim.

117
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:10,357
Press I,

118
00:06:10,357 --> 00:06:11,821
and type three lines.

119
00:06:11,821 --> 00:06:12,518
Java home,

120
00:06:12,518 --> 00:06:13,145
the path.

121
00:06:13,145 --> 00:06:13,981
Port holder,

122
00:06:13,981 --> 00:06:14,887
python3.

123
00:06:14,887 --> 00:06:16,141
And the exception,

124
00:06:16,141 --> 00:06:17,117
ZipException.

125
00:06:19,167 --> 00:06:21,791
Escape, then colon, wq, and enter.

126
00:06:23,341 --> 00:06:25,709
Run the judge.

127
00:06:26,259 --> 00:06:30,611
Five checks, five passes. Every cause found, and every fix proven.

128
00:06:31,161 --> 00:06:33,124
Clean up.

129
00:06:33,674 --> 00:06:38,751
Is the port free? Count the lines.

130
00:06:39,301 --> 00:06:44,357
Zero. Nothing listens. Three causes, found by reading, and fixed one at a time.

131
00:06:45,907 --> 00:06:48,296
Your task. Fix three faults, and prove it.

132
00:06:48,846 --> 00:06:49,784
One: lab up.

133
00:06:49,784 --> 00:06:50,800
Start Tomcat,

134
00:06:50,800 --> 00:06:52,519
and read what it says.

135
00:06:52,519 --> 00:06:55,098
Fix the cause in setenv.sh,

136
00:06:55,098 --> 00:06:55,801
with vim.

137
00:06:56,351 --> 00:06:57,471
Two: start again.

138
00:06:57,471 --> 00:06:58,393
Ask with curl,

139
00:06:58,393 --> 00:06:59,711
and see who answers.

140
00:06:59,711 --> 00:07:01,292
Find who holds the port,

141
00:07:01,292 --> 00:07:01,819
stop it,

142
00:07:01,819 --> 00:07:03,071
and restart Tomcat.

143
00:07:03,621 --> 00:07:09,189
Three: Tomcat answers, but CloudCart does not. Read the log. Put the good war in place.

144
00:07:09,739 --> 00:07:11,547
Four: write answers.txt,

145
00:07:11,547 --> 00:07:12,295
three lines.

146
00:07:12,295 --> 00:07:13,230
The wrong path,

147
00:07:13,230 --> 00:07:14,228
the port holder,

148
00:07:14,228 --> 00:07:15,350
and the exception.

149
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:18,886
Five: lab check, five checks. Then lab down.

150
00:07:20,936 --> 00:07:25,139
Here is where to find everything. Pause on this screen if you need to write it down.

151
00:07:25,689 --> 00:07:27,337
The lab lives on GitHub,

152
00:07:27,337 --> 00:07:28,504
at it-waves,

153
00:07:28,504 --> 00:07:30,083
/devops-ai,

154
00:07:30,083 --> 00:07:31,594
in the folder academy,

155
00:07:31,594 --> 00:07:32,281
/lab.

156
00:07:32,831 --> 00:07:38,228
Two files: lab116.sh, and shortcuts116.sh.

157
00:07:38,778 --> 00:07:39,697
Install it,

158
00:07:39,697 --> 00:07:42,622
on any Linux machine: sudo install,

159
00:07:42,622 --> 00:07:44,543
dash m seven five five,

160
00:07:44,543 --> 00:07:46,549
lab116.sh,

161
00:07:46,549 --> 00:07:47,802
into /usr

162
00:07:47,802 --> 00:07:48,805
/local

163
00:07:48,805 --> 00:07:49,807
/sbin.

164
00:07:50,357 --> 00:07:55,499
Load the short name with: source shortcuts116.sh. You get: lab.

165
00:07:56,049 --> 00:07:57,186
You need a JDK,

166
00:07:57,186 --> 00:07:57,520
curl,

167
00:07:57,520 --> 00:07:58,390
the ss tool,

168
00:07:58,390 --> 00:07:59,527
and python3.

169
00:07:59,527 --> 00:08:01,467
About one gigabyte of memory,

170
00:08:01,467 --> 00:08:06,350
and ports 8089 and 8099 free.

171
00:08:06,350 --> 00:08:08,023
The lab downloads Tomcat,

172
00:08:08,023 --> 00:08:08,826
and the app,

173
00:08:08,826 --> 00:08:09,361
for you.

174
00:08:09,911 --> 00:08:11,982
Lab up starts the faults for you.

175
00:08:11,982 --> 00:08:13,676
Lab check judges your work.

176
00:08:13,676 --> 00:08:15,433
Lab down removes everything.

177
00:08:15,433 --> 00:08:17,441
Only run it on your own machine.

178
00:08:19,491 --> 00:08:21,560
Pass or fail. You need all five.

179
00:08:22,110 --> 00:08:24,841
The JAVA_HOME is fixed, and Tomcat runs.

180
00:08:25,391 --> 00:08:28,399
Port 8089 belongs to Tomcat.

181
00:08:28,949 --> 00:08:31,381
CloudCart answers, and its health says up.

182
00:08:31,931 --> 00:08:34,470
The war on disk is the good, complete file.

183
00:08:35,020 --> 00:08:37,729
The three causes in answers.txt are right.

184
00:08:38,279 --> 00:08:39,580
To pass, all five.

185
00:08:41,630 --> 00:08:43,401
Your turn, on your own machine.

186
00:08:43,951 --> 00:08:48,367
One: lab up, read the task list, and start Tomcat. Read the first symptom.

187
00:08:48,917 --> 00:08:52,778
Two: fix the JAVA_HOME, with vim. Write down the wrong path first.

188
00:08:53,328 --> 00:08:57,552
Three: find the stranger on the port, stop it, and restart Tomcat.

189
00:08:58,102 --> 00:09:01,046
Four: read the log, and replace the damaged war.

190
00:09:01,596 --> 00:09:06,268
Five: write the three causes, and run lab check, until you see five out of five.

191
00:09:06,818 --> 00:09:09,399
Six: lab down, and prove the port is free.

192
00:09:09,949 --> 00:09:11,784
Pause the video, and begin now.

193
00:09:27,334 --> 00:09:28,209
Quick check.

194
00:09:28,759 --> 00:09:31,063
What are the five steps of the incident method?

195
00:09:31,613 --> 00:09:34,706
How could you tell that Tomcat was not the one answering?

196
00:09:35,256 --> 00:09:37,176
Which command shows who holds a port?

197
00:09:37,726 --> 00:09:40,393
Why did the war file fail: what did the log say?

198
00:09:40,943 --> 00:09:43,691
Objective covered: CloudCart version zero,

199
00:09:43,691 --> 00:09:45,196
run it like a customer,

200
00:09:45,196 --> 00:09:46,767
fix it like an engineer.

201
00:09:47,317 --> 00:09:49,386
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

202
00:09:59,936 --> 00:10:02,197
Next: prove it all, from a clean copy.

203
00:10:02,747 --> 00:10:06,075
If this helped, like, share and subscribe, so you do not miss it.
